	<section_number>64.2-1602</section_number>
	<catch_line>Power of attorney is durable</catch_line>
	<text>
		A power of attorney created under this chapter is durable unless it expressly provides that it is terminated by the incapacity of the principal.
	</text>
	<history>2010, cc. 455, 632, § 26-75; 2012, c. 614.</history>
</law>
